WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:16.647
My name is Frank Davis, the year is 1926, and I'm a Pullman porter.

2
00:00:16.648 --> 00:00:24.175
In 1865 a white man named George Pullman created a company that makes luxury sleeping cars for trains.

3
00:00:24.176 --> 00:00:31.910
Like a first-class hotel on wheels, each Pullman car has marble sinks, fine carpeting, and crystal lights.

4
00:00:31.911 --> 00:00:39.426
Many railroad companies include these luxury cars in their trains because people love to be pampered.

5
00:00:39.427 --> 00:00:48.823
In fact, Pullman porters are called ambassadors of hospitality because we always try to please the passengers in any way we can.

6
00:00:48.824 --> 00:00:53.417
Being a porter is one of the few good jobs a black man can get.

7
00:00:53.418 --> 00:01:04.202
Usually the Pullman Company hires black men aged 25 to 40 years old who have a high-school education, but some of the porters are college graduates.

8
00:01:04.203 --> 00:01:10.321
In fact, a few porters I work with have graduated from law and medical school.

9
00:01:10.322 --> 00:01:17.668
My uncle, who got me my job, said that 30 percent of all black doctors were once porters.

10
00:01:17.669 --> 00:01:24.703
You see, it's against the law in a lot of places for whites and blacks to work or socialize together.

11
00:01:24.704 --> 00:01:29.678
Because of this segregation, hospitals won't hire black doctors,

12
00:01:29.679 --> 00:01:36.762
so they work as porters to save enough money to open their own medical offices in black neighborhoods.

13
00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.734
If a young man wants to be a Pullman porter,

14
00:01:39.735 --> 00:01:47.088
he has to be recommended by a respected member of the black community, such as a preacher or a businessman.

15
00:01:47.089 --> 00:01:52.563
The Pullman Company really likes to hire people who have relatives that have been porters,

16
00:01:52.564 --> 00:02:00.894
because then the company knows the new porter already understands that the company is very strict, almost like the military.

17
00:02:00.895 --> 00:02:07.114
That's why Pullman porter jobs tend to run in families, from generation to generation.

18
00:02:07.115 --> 00:02:14.214
My uncle has been a porter for forty years, and my father was one too before he died a few years ago.

19
00:02:14.215 --> 00:02:22.784
New porters are given a rule book that must be followed faithfully; this book contains instructions for everything a porter does.

20
00:02:22.785 --> 00:02:29.112
In fact, every new porter has to pass a written test that proves he knows the rules.

21
00:02:29.113 --> 00:02:33.694
For instance, there is only one way to make a bed—the Pullman way.

22
00:02:33.695 --> 00:02:40.342
The sleeping cars have upper and lower beds, called berths, which look a lot like built-in bunk beds.

23
00:02:40.343 --> 00:02:46.534
The lower berth is a seat during the day, and the upper berth pulls out from the ceiling at night.

24
00:02:46.535 --> 00:02:50.479
Getting the berths ready for people to sleep in is very difficult;

25
00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:59.334
I have to fold down the seats, hang curtains for privacy, put up a headboard, and make up the bed—all in three to five minutes.

26
00:02:59.335 --> 00:03:03.352
Some older porters can do it in ninety seconds!

27
00:03:03.353 --> 00:03:06.828
It's very important to do everything exactly right,

28
00:03:06.829 --> 00:03:14.017
and I still carry the fifty-page rule book in my hip pocket to make sure I can always refer to it when I need to.

29
00:03:14.018 --> 00:03:18.983
When I was first hired, an older porter taught me everything I needed to know.

30
00:03:18.984 --> 00:03:26.100
He accompanied me at all times on my first train trips to make sure I knew how to properly fold the blankets and towels,

31
00:03:26.101 --> 00:03:30.139
dispose of dirty laundry, and wear my uniform.

32
00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:38.695
He even taught me how to gently wake the passengers by shaking the privacy curtains instead of knocking on the edge of the berth.

33
00:03:38.696 --> 00:03:45.154
I learned quickly, and my paycheck was $16 for working 73 hours my first week.

34
00:03:45.155 --> 00:03:53.795
The average pay for white men is about $19 a week for a lot fewer hours, but a black man is still lucky to have a job like this.

35
00:03:53.796 --> 00:03:56.615
Being a porter can be a demanding job:

36
00:03:56.616 --> 00:04:05.575
porters are so famous for keeping everything spotless that a magazine once said that Pullman cars are cleaner than most homes in the United States.

37
00:04:05.576 --> 00:04:10.566
The job is more than just cleaning up, making beds, and folding laundry though.

38
00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:16.106
If there aren't enough waiters in the dining room, I put on a white jacket and serve food.

39
00:04:16.107 --> 00:04:22.350
I help with luggage, clean the bathrooms, and teach the passengers about train safety.

40
00:04:22.351 --> 00:04:29.148
Porters cut hair, deliver drinks, iron clothes, and do almost everything they're asked.

41
00:04:29.149 --> 00:04:34.814
One day a passenger ripped the seat of his pants, and he didn't have another pair,

42
00:04:34.815 --> 00:04:39.899
so I cut some material from a black umbrella and sewed it over the tear.

43
00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.608
The man said it was the best sewing job he'd ever seen!

44
00:04:43.609 --> 00:04:53.249
Most of the passengers are nice and friendly, but sometimes a few of them can be a real problem, which makes a porter's job much harder.

45
00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:59.245
Some men will get into their berths with a cigarette and make a big mess with the ashes.

46
00:04:59.246 --> 00:05:05.695
Other men—we call them whitewashers—spread shaving cream all over the sink when they shave.

47
00:05:05.696 --> 00:05:12.321
Then there are the fussy ladies who never stop ringing the bell to complain about something.

48
00:05:12.322 --> 00:05:18.488
What makes it really difficult is that porters are never allowed to go off duty when they are on the train.

49
00:05:18.489 --> 00:05:25.316
We try to catch a few hours' sleep at night, but if we're needed for anything, we have to get up right away.

50
00:05:25.317 --> 00:05:30.189
Believe me, it's very tiring to work around the clock.

51
00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:39.331
Every night all the porters get together to shine shoes in the smoking room after we've collected the shoes from boxes outside the passengers' berths.

52
00:05:39.332 --> 00:05:47.244
When the people are asleep and no one is listening, we talk about the union, the Brotherhood of Sleeping Car Porters.

53
00:05:47.245 --> 00:05:55.312
It's the first black union in the United States, and some porters think that if we join the union, the company will treat us better.

54
00:05:55.313 --> 00:06:02.861
The union wants every porter to be paid more money and insists that we get at least three hours of sleep each night,

55
00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:07.762
but I worry that the company will find out I'm a union member and fire me.

56
00:06:07.763 --> 00:06:14.307
Being a Pullman porter has made the lives of my wife and son easier, and I am very thankful for that.

57
00:06:14.308 --> 00:06:20.206
But I hope my little boy will have a chance to study and become whatever he wants in life.

58
00:06:20.207 --> 00:06:27.114
I didn't have that opportunity, but maybe he will.
